§§ `The basic amount fixed for a child at a place in the parent's count`

-- (a) "for the first child and the fifth and later child in the parent's count";
-- (b) "for the second, third and fourth child in the parent's count".
-- The places are 1, 2, 3, …; (a) and (b) between them cover every place, so no third arm.
@ref National Insurance Law s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" (2)(a), (2)(b) (source lines 187-188)
GIVEN `the place` IS A NUMBER  @desc the child's place in the parent's count, 1 for the first
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph (2)(a) fixes the basic amount for the child at place` `the place` MEANS
        "(א) בעד הילד הראשון" ... `the place` EQUALS   1
    OR  "והחמישי ואילך"       ... `the place` AT LEAST 5

@ref National Insurance Law s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" (2)(a), (2)(b) (source lines 187-188)
GIVEN `the place`   IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts` IS A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic amount fixed for the child at place` `the place` `under` `the amounts` MEANS
    IF   `paragraph (2)(a) fixes the basic amount for the child at place` `the place`
    THEN `the amounts`'s `under paragraph (2)(a)`
    ELSE `the amounts`'s `under paragraph (2)(b)`

§§ `Paragraph (2)(c)`

-- "notwithstanding (a) and (b), for a benefit under the Income Support Law, or a supplement
-- under s 68(c)". Only the second use is in this row; s 68(c) reads `under paragraph (2)(c)`
-- directly (nii-s68-amount.l4). The Income Support Law is not in this row.
@ref National Insurance Law s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" (2)(c) (source line 189)
GIVEN `the amounts` IS A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic amount for a supplement under section 68(c), under` `the amounts` MEANS
    `the amounts`'s `under paragraph (2)(c)`
